 ## Secret law
-Caller-provided credential headers are forbidden. Durable request/receipt/cache/usage/telemetry records contain no secret material. SecretLease material is short-lived and closed after transport use. Complete memory zeroization of immutable Java String values is not claimed.
+Caller-provided credential headers are forbidden. Durable request/receipt/cache/usage/telemetry records contain no secret material. SecretLease material is short-lived and closed after transport use. Durable provider descriptors persist the non-secret credential prefix needed to reconstruct the exact descriptor while never persisting secret material. Complete memory zeroization of immutable Java String values is not claimed.
 
 ## Cache/source law
 Cache reuse requires exact privacy partition, freshness and RFC 9111 Vary request-value binding. Cross-provider source identities are canonicalized separately from provider hits. Search coverage must expose COMPLETE/PARTIAL/INSUFFICIENT standing rather than hiding provider failures.
